00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:15.440
Now, speaking of the Newfoundland fish sauce removal, here's something I wish someone had told me

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:22.040
early in my career. You arrive at a former fish processing facility on the Newfoundland coast where 110

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:29.780
bats of concentrated fish sauce have sat for 25 years. The phase two shows elevated BOD, ammonia,

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:36.160
and sulfide in shallow groundwater, but the nearest receptor is a small harbor 300 meters away.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:42.700
The science here is straightforward. An aerobic decomposition of proteins generates volatile fatty

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:48.460
acids and hydrogen sulfide that migrate rapidly in sandy or fractured bedrock aquifers,

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:55.060
typical of Atlantic Canada. In the field you notice that standard low flow sampling underestimates

00:04:55.060 --> 00:05:01.260
peak concentrations because the plume is density stratified. The experienced practitioner therefore

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:07.020
installs multi-level wells screened at 1 meter intervals and collects both filtered and unfiltered

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:13.900
samples for sulfide and ammonia to capture the true mass flux. Regulatory submissions under the

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:19.790
Newfoundland and Labrador Environmental Protection Act must demonstrate that post removal verification

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:27.550
meets the same risk-based criteria used for petroleum hydrocarbons, even though no CSR protocol directly

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:33.970
addresses this waste stream. The most common mistake is assuming that once the vats are hauled away,

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:40.710
the source is eliminated. Residual pooled liquid and stained soil beneath the vats continue to

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:47.570
release contaminants for months, so the fix is to require a minimum 30-day post excavation monitoring

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:53.970
period, with triggers for additional excavation or in-seat to oxidation before issuing a closure

00:05:53.970 --> 00:06:00.790
letter. If you're working on high BOD organic wastes in Atlantic Canada, you'll want to update phase

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:07.690
two sampling protocols to include multi-level wells and sulfide speciation. Brief remediation

00:06:07.690 --> 00:06:14.050
contractors on the 200 truck removal sequence completed in St. Mary's and confirmed disposal facility

00:06:14.050 --> 00:06:20.330
acceptance criteria for similar wastes. Review BC land stewardship case studies for wildfire

00:06:20.330 --> 00:06:25.350
interface risk reduction credits that may apply to current contaminated sites projects.

